# GitHub Pages Deploy

## Routing

- Always use `HashRouter` — never `BrowserRouter`
- GitHub Pages has no server-side routing; hash routes avoid 404s on refresh/deep links

## Vite base path

- Keep `base` in `vite.config.js` set to `/<repo-name>/` (e.g. `/Portfolio/`)
- Use relative or base-aware asset paths so builds work under the project subdirectory

## Deployment

- Deploy with the official GitHub Pages Actions workflow on push to `main`
- Do not use the `gh-pages` branch or the `gh-pages` npm package

## Safety

- Never commit secrets or credentials
- No server-side code — this is a static client-only site
